Description: Do not show the splash screen under Wayland
 The splash is a top level window that places itself over the main window and
 asks to stay on top, neither of which a Wayland client can do, so the
 compositor puts it behind the main window where it is a stray window rather
 than a cover. The canvas renders its own loading screen, which the preceding
 patch presents before the blocking start up work, so nothing is lost. X11 is
 unchanged.
